      "text": "<h2>Overview</h2><p>Mega Raichu X, is the slightly tankier counterpart to Mega Raichu Y. It doesn't have as strong raid value however there is hope with how volt tackle+ is adjusted. Because the moveset is the exact same as Mega Raichu Y, the meta strategy for this guide is virtually identical.</p><h4>Est Time to Win: 200.5s - 240.5s</h4><h2>Main Strategy</h2><p>Utilizing Primal Groudon, comfortably DPS Mega Raichu per cycle until Primal Groudon requires healing. Be mindful to <a href=\"https://soloraidarchive.github.io/solo-raid-mechanics.html#strategy-clean-exit\" target=\"_blank\">exit the fight </a>without having leftover energy as this would lower DPS significantly if repeated too often.</p><p><br></p><p>Mega Raichu X has 1 counter point to Primal Groudon in learning Surf. As a result if it learns Surf, it is recommended to add additional ground attackers. Lots of damage &amp; energy will be absorbed from surf so it is wise to not over extend using each attacker. A recommended strategy is <a href=\"https://soloraidarchive.github.io/solo-raid-mechanics.html#strategy-hot-swap\" target=\"_blank\">swapping</a> to the next attacker when below 25-30% health.</p>",
